 "method": [
  "Each model's mean of its monthly values (months weighted equally, as in the Atlas) over 1995-2014 in the historical run and over 2021-2040, 2041-2060 and 2081-2100 in each SSP run, cell by cell; a mean needs 80% of its months.",
  "Change: the SSP mean minus the same model's 1995-2014 mean (t, txx), or their ratio as % change (pr; none for a model whose 1995-2014 mean is under 0.1 mm a day). Only models with both runs count, as in the Atlas.",
  "Percentiles across models by linear interpolation (numpy 'linear', R type 7); none where fewer than 10 models have a value.",
  "The app adds the change to the place's observed 1995-2014 mean (rain: times 1 + change / 100), the delta method; raw model values are never put next to observations."
 ],
 "notes": [
  "One member per model, as the Atlas provides; the model lists differ by variable and scenario (see models).",
  "txx is the hottest day of each month, matching the app's hottest day of the month; its change is not the change of the annual maximum.",
  "Every cell is stored, ocean included (the Atlas files hold values everywhere); land says which cells are land.",
  "CAMS-CSM1-0 and IITM-ESM lack 2100 (IITM-ESM also 2099 in SSP3-7.0); their 2081-2100 means use the months present."
 ],
 "self_checks": [
  "t historical: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (35 of 35)",
  "t ssp126: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (32 of 32)",
  "t ssp245: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (34 of 34)",
  "t ssp370: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (30 of 30)",
  "t ssp585: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (34 of 34)",
  "txx historical: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (28 of 28)",
  "txx ssp126: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (26 of 26)",
  "txx ssp245: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (27 of 27)",
  "txx ssp370: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (23 of 23)",
  "txx ssp585: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (27 of 27)",
  "pr historical: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (34 of 34)",
  "pr ssp126: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (31 of 31)",
  "pr ssp245: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (32 of 32)",
  "pr ssp370: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (28 of 28)",
  "pr ssp585: each model's mean at 40.5N 74.5W equals the OPeNDAP point series (33 of 33)",
  "t: 10th <= 50th <= 90th percentile wherever there are percentiles (100.0% of scenario x window x cell)",
  "txx: 10th <= 50th <= 90th percentile wherever there are percentiles (100.0% of scenario x window x cell)",
  "pr: 10th <= 50th <= 90th percentile wherever there are percentiles (99.0% of scenario x window x cell)",
  "t 2081-2100 median change, area-weighted world mean [1.07, 2.01, 2.99, 3.87] degC, rises with the scenario",
  "t SSP5-8.5 2081-2100 world mean of the median change 3.87 degC lies in 2.5-5.5 (CMIP6)"
 ],
